WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.920
New York, March 2024.

2
00:00:02.920 --> 00:00:06.200
On the futures market,
cocoa breaks a record.

3
00:00:06.200 --> 00:00:08.780
For the first time, a metric ton of cocoa

4
00:00:08.780 --> 00:00:11.460
costs more than 10,000 dollars.

5
00:00:11.460 --> 00:00:14.270
The price has roughly
doubled since January.

6
00:00:14.270 --> 00:00:17.960
Every grower on the planet is
getting the same loud message:

7
00:00:17.960 --> 00:00:21.210
supply more. So when prices jump,

8
00:00:21.210 --> 00:00:24.090
why can some producers flood
the market while others

9
00:00:24.090 --> 00:00:26.200
cannot grow more for years?

10
00:00:26.200 --> 00:00:29.920
In this mission, you'll calculate
price elasticity of supply,

11
00:00:29.920 --> 00:00:31.980
including with the midpoint method.

12
00:00:31.980 --> 00:00:34.570
Then you'll shift demand
on a supply and demand

13
00:00:34.570 --> 00:00:37.430
graph and see how much
becomes a higher price,

14
00:00:37.430 --> 00:00:39.620
and how much becomes more output.

15
00:00:39.620 --> 00:00:43.310
Your mission: figure out what
holds some producers back.
